OpenUA for Atari System V
=========================

OpenUA is an open engine for SSI's Unlimited Adventures (FRUA, 1993). This
package is its AMIX build, for Atari System V on the TT030 with the
service pack (github.com/slaapliedje/atari-sysv-sp1): it needs the amx
module, X11R6.3 with Xatw, and xatwrun, which the service pack's card has.

It installs:

  /opt/openua/bin/openua      the game
  /opt/openua/bin/uagame      runs it full screen at 640x480 on a second
                              X server (Ctrl+Alt+F1 desktop, F2 the game)
  /opt/openua/bin/ua-getdata  copies the game data from a PC
  /opt/openua/doc/            this file and the licence (GPL-2.0)

The game data is NOT in the package: it is SSI's, and you need your own
copy of Unlimited Adventures (the DOS release works).


Install
-------

As root on the TT, with the package copied over:

    pkgadd -d /var/tmp/openua-VERSION.pkg OPENUA

Remove it with `pkgrm OPENUA` (the game data in your home stays).


The game data
-------------

1. On the PC, in a clone of OpenUA (github.com/slaapliedje/OpenUA), stage
   the data from your DOS install, as for the Atari builds:

       make -o frua.prg gamedata-dos DOS_DIR=/path/to/FRUA GAMEDATA_DIR=/path/to/stage

   frua.rsc is made from your CKIT.EXE and the art, sounds and music
   are converted (Python 3 is all it needs; `-o frua.prg` skips building
   the Atari program, which the TT has no use for).

2. Serve it to the TT (read-only, until Ctrl-C):

       tools/ua-serve.sh /path/to/stage

   It prints the command to run on the TT. UA_ALLOW=192.168.3.0/24 in
   front of it limits who may connect.

3. On the TT, as the user who will play:

       /opt/openua/bin/ua-getdata PC-ADDRESS

   The data goes to $HOME/openua (or $OPENUA_DATA, or a directory given as
   the second argument). Running it again copies only what changed and
   deletes nothing, so saved games stay.

   It needs the service pack's rsync from after 2026-11-24: the one before
   could not connect to a numeric address ("getaddrinfo: ... Unknown
   host"). With that one, give the PC a name in /etc/hosts and use it.


Play
----

From a terminal on the desktop, `/opt/openua/bin/uagame`. For a button on
the panel, right-click the panel, Add..., with the command
/opt/openua/bin/uagame and the game icon.

Settings, all optional, in the environment:

  OPENUA_DATA      where the game data is (default $HOME/openua)
  OPENUA_WINDOW=1  a window on the desktop instead of full screen
  OPENUA_VOLUME=N  the sound driver's volume, 0..40
